        <title type="html"><![CDATA[docs: change inline style example to avoid confusion]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43775</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43775"/>
        <updated>2026-04-13T23:32:20.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62723358?u=f3632393d0193c912fa572def786f97a3e49c40b&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">On <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Security-Policy/style-src-attr#violation_cases" rel="nofollow">Content-Security-Policy: style-src-attr directive &gt; Examples &gt; Violation cases</a>, change the style attribute value to something that does not use a keyword.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">I intend to avoid possible confusion. A user might think <code class="notranslate">style-src-attr 'none'</code> blocks <code class="notranslate">&lt;div style="display:none"&gt;Foo&lt;/div&gt;</code> because it has "none" in the attribute value. (At least one user was confused… me.)</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto">N/A</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto">N/A</p>]]></content>
